# Repeated terrain symbols

Render terrain-specific symbols on every applied terrain hex while retaining the matching symbols in the radial selector.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Brick, Ore, Wheat, Lumber, Wool, Desert, and Ocean each use an appropriate distinct symbol.
- [x] Several copies of the terrain symbol are distributed across each hex.
- [x] Symbols render at approximately 50% opacity behind number tokens.
- [x] Numbers, pips, pieces, placement targets, and radial controls remain legible above the symbols.
- [x] Rendering remains stable while zooming, panning, and editing terrain.
- [ ] Focused rendering checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Verification

- Add view/rendering coverage for terrain-to-symbol mapping and manually check representative numbered and unnumbered hexes.

## Evidence

- Added distinct domain symbol mappings for all seven terrain cases and a fixed six-copy count.
- Hex rendering uses six normalized positions clipped to the hex, with each symbol at 50% opacity beneath number tokens and all Board-piece/interaction layers.
- Inset the normalized positions further from the hex boundary so faded symbols retain visible edge breathing room.
- Terrain radial choices reuse the same symbol mapping over their matching terrain colour.
- Removed the separate single Ocean icon so every terrain follows one deterministic rendering path.
- Added domain regression coverage for distinct non-empty mappings and the six-copy contract.
- The app, unit-test, and UI-test bundles compile using `/private/tmp/Catanalyst-tasks018-024-derived`.

## Remaining manual verification

- Confirm symbol contrast, number/pip readability, and visual density for all terrains on a functioning simulator/device.
